# Materials Science Taste Considerations & Philosophical Probes
#
# Solid-state aesthetics, defect philosophies, the ethics of extraction, and wonder probes across materials science.

#>spw_cache_univ_mse_taste
#:cache #!materials_science
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Synthesize the aesthetic sensibilities, defect ontologies, and ecological-ethical responsibilities that define Materials Science and Engineering."
  ~#resonance: "Crystallographic symmetry, the poetry of crystalline imperfection, sub-Angstrom observation, and materials circularity"
}

^["the_reverence_for_the_solid_state"]{
  ontological_beauty: "A solid crystal is not dead inert rock; it is a dynamic, shimmering cathedral of quantum wavefunctions bound together in perfect geometric harmony."
  aesthetic_dimensions: #[
    "Translational Invariance: The breathtaking concept that fourteen simple Bravais lattice geometries can tile three-dimensional space infinitely to generate millions of distinct crystalline minerals",
    "Reciprocal Space Duality: The realization that direct real-space atomic lattices and reciprocal momentum-space diffraction spheres are Fourier duals of one another, each containing the whole truth of matter",
    "The Thermodynamic Dance: How enthalpy strives to lock atoms into rigid order while entropy fights to shake them into chaos, with the Gibbs free energy orchestrating their delicate compromise"
  ]
}

^["the_philosophy_of_the_defect"]{
  paradox_of_imperfection: "In materials science, perfection is sterile and weak; virtue and utility reside exclusively in the flaw."
  defect_truths: #[
    "The Soul of Metal: Pure, dislocation-free iron whiskers are brittle and fracture catastrophically; real structural steel can bend, absorb impact, and endure because billions of line defects (dislocations) glide and dissipate energy",
    "The Light of the Dopant: Pure intrinsic silicon is an uninteresting electrical insulator; adding one boron atom per million silicon atoms transforms it into the microchip that runs modern human civilization",
    "The Color of the Gem: Pure aluminum oxide (corundum) is completely colorless; a trace impurity of chromium atoms absorbs yellow-green light to birth the fiery red brilliance of a ruby"
  ]
}

^["the_ethics_of_materials_extraction_and_entropy"]{
  ecological_gravity: "Every advanced technological artifact—from an electric vehicle battery to a quantum qubit—demands rare elements dug from the crust of the Earth."
  ethical_imperatives: #[
    "The Human Cost of the Elements: Remembering that cobalt, lithium, and rare earths carry heavy human rights and ecological footprints; designing alloys that avoid conflict minerals",
    "Thermodynamic Circularity: Acknowledging that recycling an alloy is a battle against the second law of thermodynamics; engineering alloys designed for single-pot disassembly and closed-loop pyrometallurgical sorting",
    "Embodied Energy in Infrastructure: Recognizing that steel and cement production alone account for nearly 15% of global greenhouse emissions; material scientists hold the direct keys to global industrial decarbonization"
  ]
}

^"taste"{
  ~#taste: "Materials science is the humble realization that human civilization does not advance by ideas alone, but by our ability to coax atoms into holding together under stress."
  ~#wonder: "Can materials science design structural alloys that repair their own fatigue cracks at ambient temperatures, rendering structural mechanical failure extinct?"
}

^"invariants"{
  "Materials engineering must account for the complete environmental lifecycle and raw material supply chain of proposed compositions.",
  "Structural integrity claims must explicitly incorporate the worst-case statistical distribution of microstructural defects (Weibull modulus analysis).",
  "Scientists and engineers must never separate the aesthetic beauty of an advanced material from the ethical reality of its mining and disposal.",
}

#>wonder_mse_taste_1
?["Can a bio-inspired multi-scale ceramic composite achieve the fracture toughness of titanium while remaining 100% recyclable?"]{
  #:depth #!materials ~#lens(biomimetic_toughening)
  ~#hypothesis: "Brick-and-mortar microstructures mimicking natural nacre (mother-of-pearl) synthesized using water-soluble sacrificial biopolymers achieve K_IC fracture toughness exceeding 25 MPa*m^(1/2) while dissolving in warm enzymatic baths at end-of-life for total mineral recovery."
  !probe{ "Measure R-curve crack resistance and closed-loop mineral recovery yield in freeze-cast alumina-chitosan nacre mimetics." }
  $%[fracture.r_curve_toughening_mpa_m, recycling.mineral_recovery_yield_percent]
}

#>wonder_mse_taste_2
?["What is the fundamental thermodynamic limit of grain boundary stability against thermal coarsening in nanocrystalline metals?"]{
  #:depth #!physical ~#lens(nanocrystalline_thermodynamics)
  ~#hypothesis: "Nanocrystalline grain sizes (< 10 nm) can be indefinitely stabilized against grain growth at 0.9 Tm by selecting solute segregants whose enthalpy of grain boundary segregation exactly offsets the positive grain boundary excess free energy, driving effective interface energy to zero."
  !probe{ "Track grain size stability in tungsten-titanium and copper-tantalum nanocrystalline alloys annealed for 1,000 hours at 1,000 degrees Celsius using in-situ TEM." }
  $%[nanocrystals.grain_size_nanometers, thermodynamics.interface_excess_free_energy]
}
